completions_2:
Jon drives 100 miles a day for 30 days, so he drives a total of 100 miles/day * 30 days = 3000 miles in a month.

His car needs a tune-up every 1000 miles. To find out how many tune-ups he needs in that time, we divide the total miles driven by the interval between tune-ups: 3000 miles / 1000 miles/tune-up = 3 tune-ups.

\boxed{3}

